# 10. Resource Synchronization

## 10.1 Initial Synchronization

After pairing, Aura should load all required bridge resources before marking the integration ready.

Required initial data may include:

- Bridge metadata
- Devices
- Lights
- Grouped lights
- Rooms
- Zones
- Scenes
- Sensors
- Buttons
- Entertainment configurations

## 10.2 Synchronization Stages

```text
Connecting
↓
Authenticating
↓
Loading bridge metadata
↓
Loading resources
↓
Mapping capabilities
↓
Subscribing to events
↓
Ready
```

## 10.3 Partial Synchronization

A partial failure should not make the entire bridge unusable.

For example, if entertainment configurations fail to load but lights succeed, standard lighting control should remain available.

The repository should track synchronization state per resource category.

## 10.4 Resource Identity

Aura should preserve stable mappings between Hue resource IDs and Aura entity IDs.

Suggested identity format:

```text
hue:<bridge-id>:<resource-type>:<resource-id>
```

This identifier is internal and should not be shown to users.

