# 18. Scenes

## 18.1 Hue Scene Import

Aura should import compatible Hue scenes as external scene actions.

Imported scenes should include:

- Scene name
- Associated room or zone
- Supported target lights
- Dynamic capability where available
- Last known availability

## 18.2 Aura Scene Integration

Hue actions should be first-class steps in Aura Scene Engine.

Example:

```text
Movie Night
├── Wake Apple TV
├── Turn on Philips TV
├── Select HDMI input
├── Activate Hue scene “Cinema”
├── Set hallway lights to 15%
└── Set HomePod volume
```

The Hue plugin should provide scene actions such as:

- Activate Hue scene
- Set room state
- Set zone state
- Set individual light state
- Start dynamic scene
- Stop dynamic scene

## 18.3 Scene Execution

Grouped Hue commands should be executed as close together as possible.

Aura Scene Engine should not serialize independent Hue commands unnecessarily.

## 18.4 Scene Failure

A partial Hue scene failure must be reported to the Scene Engine with per-action results.

Example:

```swift
enum SceneActionResult {
    case success
    case partialSuccess(details: [ActionFailure])
    case failure(AuraError)
}
```

---

# 19. Dynamic Scenes

Where supported, Aura may expose dynamic scene controls:

- Start
- Pause
- Resume
- Stop
- Adjust speed if supported

Dynamic scene state should be event-driven where possible.

If dynamic control is unavailable, Aura should still allow standard scene activation.

