# 32. Swift Architecture

Recommended types:

```text
HueBridgePlugin
HueBridgeDiscoveryService
HuePairingCoordinator
HueAPIClient
HueEventStreamClient
HueRepository
HueResourceStore
HueDeviceMapper
HueRoomMapper
HueSceneAdapter
HueCommandCoordinator
HueColorConverter
HueDiagnosticsService
HueCredentialStore
```

## 32.1 Plugin Protocol

```swift
protocol AuraDevicePlugin: Sendable {
    var identifier: String { get }

    func discover() -> AsyncStream<DiscoveredDevice>
    func pair(with candidate: DiscoveredDevice) async throws
    func synchronize() async throws
    func devices() async -> [AuraDevice]
    func execute(_ command: AuraCommand) async throws -> CommandResult
    func diagnostics() async -> PluginDiagnostics
}
```

## 32.2 Repository Actor

```swift
actor HueRepository {
    private var resources: [HueResourceID: HueResource] = [:]
    private var pendingCommands: [CommandID: PendingCommand] = [:]

    func synchronize() async throws
    func apply(event: HueEvent) async
    func execute(_ command: HueCommand) async throws -> CommandResult
    func snapshot() -> HueRepositorySnapshot
}
```

The actor should protect resource state and command coordination from data races.

## 32.3 Dependency Injection

The plugin should receive interfaces rather than constructing concrete dependencies internally.

```swift
struct HuePluginDependencies {
    let discovery: HueBridgeDiscovering
    let apiClientFactory: HueAPIClientFactory
    let credentialStore: HueCredentialStoring
    let clock: AuraClock
    let logger: AuraLogging
}
```

---

# 33. Concurrency Rules

- Networking must use Swift concurrency
- No bridge request may block the main actor
- UI updates must be delivered on the appropriate actor
- Long-lived event streams must support cancellation
- Pairing attempts must be cancellable
- Slider command tasks must cancel stale values
- Repository state must be isolated
- Reconnect loops must stop when the plugin is deactivated

---

# 34. Logging

Logs should use structured categories:

- hue.discovery
- hue.pairing
- hue.api
- hue.events
- hue.mapping
- hue.commands
- hue.scenes
- hue.diagnostics

Logs must never include:

- Application keys
- Authorization headers
- Full raw payloads containing sensitive identifiers
- User-created room or scene names in analytics

Debug builds may support deeper local logging with explicit developer controls.

---

# 35. Accessibility and UI Requirements

Hue controls must:

- Support VoiceOver
- Expose meaningful control labels
- Announce confirmed changes where appropriate
- Use more than color alone to represent state
- Respect Reduce Motion
- Support Dynamic Type
- Provide large touch targets
- Maintain sufficient contrast

A color control should announce a human-readable color approximation rather than raw RGB or XY values.

