# 38. Acceptance Criteria

The Hue integration is ready for initial release when all of the following are true:

- Aura discovers a local Hue Bridge v2 automatically
- A user can pair by pressing the physical bridge button
- Credentials are stored securely in Keychain
- Paired bridges reconnect after app relaunch
- Bridge IP changes are recovered through rediscovery
- Lights are mapped into Aura devices
- Hue rooms can be mapped to Aura rooms
- Zones are represented without incorrectly becoming rooms
- Individual lights can be turned on and off
- Brightness can be adjusted smoothly
- Color temperature is supported where available
- Color control is supported where available
- Grouped room control uses grouped resources where possible
- Hue scenes can be activated from Aura
- Hue actions can be added to Aura Scenes
- Event-stream updates refresh UI state
- Polling fallback works after event-stream failure
- Unreachable devices do not disable the entire bridge
- Unsupported controls are hidden
- Network and authentication errors are user-friendly
- Diagnostics expose bridge health without exposing secrets
- Core behavior is covered by automated tests
- Real hardware tests pass on the target Hue Bridge

